 "about_text": "Kana Kawanishi Gallery is a Tokyo contemporary art gallery led by director Kana Kawanishi, operating two exhibition spaces in the city: a gallery in Kiyosumi‑Shirakawa and a photography‑focused space, Kana Kawanishi Photography, in Nishi‑Azabu. The gallery represents a roster of mostly Japanese artists working across photography, painting, sculpture and mixed‑media installation, alongside a smaller group of international artists, including Finnish photographers. Its program mixes solo and group exhibitions with an active presence at international art fairs such as NADA New York, Frieze Seoul, Unseen Amsterdam, Photo London and Photo Basel, as well as Tokyo‑based fairs like Hibiya Okuroji and Art Fair Tokyo. The gallery also runs an affiliated art office handling publication, translation and editorial projects for artists and institutions.",
